PART B: WHY j>=D/14? At tau*=j/D with binding pair (1,w), w=D-1.
 ||1*tau*||=j/D (the unit runner). ||w*tau*||=||(D-1)j/D||=||-j/D||=j/D. matched.
 Need j/D>=1/14 i.e. 14j>=D=w+1. The OTHER 11 runners (2..12) must also clear j/D.
 The binding LEVEL is set by unit runner (1) and parked runner (w) TOGETHER.
 The covering obligation q=14 (only w is mult of 14) is what put w=14m in the set;
 w=14m makes D=14m+1 and the question is whether j can be as small as ceil((w+1)/14)=m+1.
